{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1384,
 "dur": 46.115,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Big Lou's stolen pie car drove straight through his own barn.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.062
  },
  {
   "text": "He'd swapped its cone-shaped wheels for flat ones. \"Easy as pie!\" So why are train wheels cones?",
   "s": 3.262,
   "e": 7.971
  },
  {
   "text": "The plan: with flat wheels, the pie car would get stuck at Hairpin Bend.",
   "s": 8.271,
   "e": 11.397
  },
  {
   "text": "Fennel the fox only wanted one cherry pie. He'd picked it out a week ago.",
   "s": 11.597,
   "e": 15.062
  },
  {
   "text": "Then the Pie Express hit the bend. The pie car screeched, threw sparks, and climbed the rail like a cat up a curtain.",
   "s": 15.262,
   "e": 20.486
  },
  {
   "text": "It ignored the bend and rolled straight across Moo Meadow, past three confused cows.",
   "s": 20.686,
   "e": 24.861
  },
  {
   "text": "Lou cheered. \"Easy as pie!\" Then he saw where it was going.",
   "s": 25.061,
   "e": 27.568
  },
  {
   "text": "So what do cone wheels do?",
   "s": 27.768,
   "e": 28.92
  },
  {
   "text": "Each wheel is fatter on the inside. On a bend, the axle slides out a little.",
   "s": 29.22,
   "e": 32.799
  },
  {
   "text": "The outer wheel rides its fat part, the inner wheel its thin part, so the axle steers itself.",
   "s": 33.199,
   "e": 37.777
  },
  {
   "text": "It's how a paper cup rolls in a circle.",
   "s": 37.977,
   "e": 39.688
  },
  {
   "text": "Flat wheels can't steer. They only know straight.",
   "s": 39.888,
   "e": 41.651
  },
  {
   "text": "Fennel got his pie. Lou got the other forty-nine. Easy as pie.",
   "s": 41.851,
   "e": 44.815
  }
 ],
